description: "Essays on consciousness, leadership, and what happens in sales rooms that the deck doesn't capture. Field Notes by Chris McCann."
ogDescription: "The room shifts when you walk in. You know this. What the quarterly review doesn't measure."
canonicalUrl: "/field-notes/"
permalink: /field-notes/index.html
---
{%- extends "base.njk" -%}

{% block head %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Blog",
    "name": "Field Notes by Chris McCann",
    "url": "https://chrismccann.co/field-notes",
    "description": "The room shifts when you walk in. You know this. What the quarterly review doesn't measure.",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Chris McCann",
      "url": "https://chrismccann.co"
    }
  }
  </script>
{% endblock %}

{% block header %}
  <header class="fade-in">
    <h1 class="page-title">Field Notes</h1>
    <div class="subhead">What the quarterly review doesn't measure.</div>
  </header>

  <div class="divider fade-in"><span class="colophon"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="6" y="0" width="8.49" height="8.49" rx="1" transform="rotate(45 6 0)" fill="none" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="1"/></svg></span></div>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <main id="main-content" class="fade-in">

    <div class="fade-in" style="border-left: 2px solid var(--black); padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <p style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--gray); letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">New here?</p>
      <p style="margin: 0;"><a class="inline-link" href="/field-notes/the-room-knew-first/">The Room Knew First</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="fade-in" style="margin: 0 0 2.5rem; padding: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--light-gray); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--light-gray); text-align: center;">
      <p style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Field Notes</p>
      <p style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.05rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--black); margin-bottom: 0.3rem; max-width: 420px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; line-height: 1.6;">Consciousness. Leadership. The gap between them.</p>
      <p style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 0.875rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--gray); opacity: 0.75; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">Twice a month.</p>
      <form id="topSubscribe" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 0; max-width: 380px; width: 100%;">
        <input type="email" id="topEmail" required placeholder="Your email" aria-label="Email address"
          style="flex: 1; padding: 10px 14px; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; border: 1px solid var(--light-gray); border-right: none; background: #fff; color: var(--black); outline: none; min-width: 0;">
        <button type="submit" id="topSubBtn"
          style="padding: 10px 20px; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--black); color: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--black); cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; transition: opacity 0.2s;">I'm in</button>
      </form>
      <div id="topSubSuccess" style="display: none; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 0.5rem;">You're in. Check your inbox.</div>
      <div id="topSubError" style="display: none; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: #c0392b; margin-top: 0.5rem;">Something went wrong. Try again.</div>
      <script>
      document.getElementById('topSubscribe').addEventListener('submit', async function(e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        const email = document.getElementById('topEmail').value.trim();
        const btn = document.getElementById('topSubBtn');
        if (!email) return;
        btn.textContent = '...';
        btn.disabled = true;
        try {
          const res = await fetch('/.netlify/functions/subscribe', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ email: email })
          });
          if (res.ok) {
            document.getElementById('topSubscribe').style.display = 'none';
            document.getElementById('topSubSuccess').style.display = 'block';
          } else {
            document.getElementById('topSubError').style.display = 'block';
            btn.textContent = 'I\'m in';
            btn.disabled = false;
          }
        } catch (err) {
          document.getElementById('topSubError').style.display = 'block';
          btn.textContent = 'I\'m in';
          btn.disabled = false;
        }
      });
      </script>
    </div>

    <section class="article-list">
      <div class="article-item" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <h3 class="theme-label">I think I might be the variable</h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">The strategy hasn't changed. The effort is there. But something in how I'm showing up stopped working, and the usual fixes aren't touching it.</p>
        <p><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> <a href="/field-notes/your-body-knows-before-you-do/">Your Body Knows Before You Do</a></p>
        <p><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> <a href="/field-notes/you-dont-need-ayahuasca/">You Don't Need Ayahuasca. You Need to Pay Attention.</a></p>
        <p><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> <a href="/field-notes/the-space-i-didnt-ask-for/">The Space I Didn't Ask For</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <h3 class="theme-label">The team has gone somewhere I can't reach</h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Same people, same agenda. The nods are there. Something else isn't. The gap between what's being said and what's actually happening keeps widening.</p>
        <p><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> <a href="/field-notes/youre-new-were-burnt-out/">You're New. We're Burnt Out.</a></p>
        <p><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> <a href="/field-notes/the-one-minute-test/">The One-Minute Test</a></p>
        <p><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span> <a href="/field-notes/the-95-percent-lie/">The 95% Lie</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="article-list">
      <h2 class="section-label">In the room</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">Leadership, teams, the observable patterns. Where most readers find their way in.</p>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">May 2026</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/the-room-knew-first/">The Room Knew First</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">A Tuesday in Q3. A rep closed the biggest deal in company history. The celebration was real. The room felt empty. This is where Field Notes started, and why.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">September 2025</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/the-95-percent-lie/">The 95% Lie</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">You've heard the stat: 95% of AI projects fail. Cue the panic. But ERP systems had 70–90% failure rates in the '90s. Every big shift starts ugly. AI isn't broken. What's broken is trying to bolt it onto organizations built for another decade.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">August 2025</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/the-one-minute-test/">The One-Minute Test</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">If you had sixty seconds to give someone feedback that could change the trajectory of their career, could you do it? Without crushing them? Most leaders can't.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">July 2025</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/youre-new-were-burnt-out/">You're New. We're Burnt Out.</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">PowerPoints full of vision. Words like 'elevate' and 'excellence' tossed around like cilantro. You bring a 30/60/90. We bring trauma, duct tape, and a team watching with crossed arms.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="article-list">
      <h2 class="section-label">The search</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">What transition costs. The questions that show up after the meeting ends.</p>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">April 2025</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/the-space-i-didnt-ask-for/">The Space I Didn't Ask For</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">No title. No team. No calendar full of meetings. Just space, uncertainty, and a quiet sense that I should be doing something. I've never not worked.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">January 2025</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/what-failure-actually-costs/">What Failure Actually Costs</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">Sometimes the breakdown isn't the end. It's the turning point. But nobody talks about what it actually costs to get there.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">March 2024</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/sales-leadership-and-the-search/">Sales Leadership and the Search</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">Beyond the labels, there's a part of me that's been searching for something I couldn't name. This is where that search started to get honest.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">October 2023</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/only-as-good-as-your-last-deal/">Only As Good As Your Last Deal</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">There's an old belief in sales that your value resets with every deal. I lived inside that belief for years. It nearly ate me.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">September 2023</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/the-call-of-the-wild/">The Call of the Wild</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">After a rough August, I went to Glacier National Park. What I found there wasn't insight. It was space.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="article-list">
      <h2 class="section-label">What's underneath</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">Consciousness, attention, identity. The deeper territory.</p>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">February 2026</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/your-body-knows-before-you-do/">Your Body Knows Before You Do</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">The hyper-vigilant Sunday night dread that meds and sleep can't fix. The tightness before Monday's meeting. Your body noticed months ago. You just weren't paying attention.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">January 2026</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/you-dont-need-ayahuasca/">You Don't Need Ayahuasca. You Need to Pay Attention.</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">Executives fly somewhere expensive to find themselves, have the breakthrough, post the cryptic Instagram story. Then they jump on the 405 and nothing changes. Recalibration doesn't require a plane ticket.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="article-item">
        <div class="article-date">August 2023</div>
        <h3><a href="/field-notes/in-the-fog/">In the Fog</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">Since my diagnosis of Bipolar II, I've learned to recognize the signs. Before that, these feelings were hidden behind performance and coffee and the next meeting.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
{% endblock %}

{% block subscribe %}
  <div class="signup-section fade-in">
    <h2 style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 1.2rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">The Field Assessment</h2>
    <p style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 16px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; max-width: 500px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; line-height: 1.6;">Eighteen questions. Five minutes. Two parts. What you&rsquo;re carrying into the room. What the room is doing with it.</p>
    <a class="cta-btn" href="/field-assessment/" style="background: var(--white); color: var(--black); border-color: var(--white);">Take the Assessment</a>
  </div>

  <section class="fade-in" style="max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2rem;">
    <div class="article-list">
      <h2 class="section-label">Earlier Work</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem;">Where this started. The voice has evolved. The questions haven't.</p>

      <h3 class="theme-label">On State &amp; Self-Awareness</h3>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/how-determine-your-values-chris-mccann" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How to Determine Your Values</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">I spent years leading without knowing what I actually stood for.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="theme-label">On Leading Differently</h3>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/end-boss-culture-chris-mccann-clbdc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The End of Boss Culture</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">The workforce doesn't want bosses. They want leaders.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/more-overlords-chris-mccann-mqhgc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">No More Overlords</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">People don't want more oversight. They want something real. Leaders, not bosses. Guides, not gatekeepers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/when-leader-changes-shouldnt-change-too-chris-mccann-plotc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">When the Leader Changes, Shouldn't They Change Too?</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">There's a missing perspective: when we as leaders are hired, how do we adapt to the teams we inherit?</p>
      </div>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/empathetic-leadership-key-unlocking-authentic-influence-chris-mccann-eoxbc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Empathetic Leadership</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">The leaders who actually shift rooms aren't performing authority. They're present.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="theme-label">On the Search</h3>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/leadership-entangled-discovering-parallels-between-quantum-mccann" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Leadership Entangled: Quantum Theory and Leadership</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">How particles stay connected across distance. Teams do the same thing. We just don't have language for it yet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/art-zen-sales-leadership-how-remove-expectations-achieve-chris-mccann-1f" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Art of Zen Sales Leadership</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">Quotas, pipeline, forecast calls. And then the Tao Te Ching on my nightstand. Two worlds that shouldn't fit together.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/sales-leadership-cosmic-dance-how-tango-paradoxes-win-chris-mccann" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sales Leadership and the Cosmic Dance</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">I stopped trying to resolve the tension and started working inside it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/yin-tonic-leading-empathy-chris-mccann" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Yin and Tonic: Leading with Empathy</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">There's another dimension to sales leadership. Quieter, harder to measure, and essential.</p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="theme-label">On Failure &amp; Transition</h3>
      <div class="article-item">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/living-life-beyond-platitudes-path-impactful-chris-mccann" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Living a Life Beyond Platitudes</a></h3>
        <p class="article-excerpt">The gap between what we say and what we actually do. That gap is where leadership lives.</p>
      </div>

      <p style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a class="inline-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/newsletters/field-notes-7050474114494451713/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View full archive on LinkedIn &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

